Here is a complete implementation of the custom web component `x-details` using the Shadow DOM, fulfilling all your requirements.

### `x-details.js`

```javascript
/**
 * x-details: A custom component similar to <details>,
 * but always shows an introductory part when collapsed.
 */
class XDetails extends HTMLElement {
    constructor() {
        super();
        // Attach Shadow DOM
        this.attachShadow({ mode: 'open' });
        this._expanded = false;

        // Initial setup of the Shadow DOM structure
        this.render();
    }

    // Lifecycle callback when the element is added to the DOM
    connectedCallback() {
        // Event listeners for the expand/collapse action
        this.shadowRoot.querySelector('.toggle-button').addEventListener('click', () => {
            this._expanded = !this._expanded;
            this.updateView();
        });

        // Initial render based on default state (collapsed)
        this.updateView();
    }

    // Renders the basic structure into the shadow root
    render() {
        this.shadowRoot.innerHTML = `
            <style>
                :host {
                    display: block;
                    border: 1px solid #ddd;
                    margin-bottom: 10px;
                    border-radius: 4px;
                    background-color: #fff;
                }
                .header-container {
                    display: flex;
                    align-items: center;
                    padding: 12px 15px;
                    cursor: pointer;
                    background-color: #f7f7f7;
                    border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;
                }
                .toggle-icon {
                    font-size: 1.2em;
                    font-weight: bold;
                    margin-right: 10px;
                    width: 20px; /* Fixed width for alignment */
                    text-align: center;
                }
                .header-text {
                    font-size: 1.1em;
                    font-weight: 600;
                    flex-grow: 1;
                }
                .content-wrapper {
                    padding: 0 15px 15px 15px;
                }
                .intro-part {
                    margin-bottom: 15px;
                    padding-bottom: 15px;
                    border-bottom: 1px dashed #eee;
                }
                .details-part {
                    padding-top: 10px;
                }
                .expand-button {
                    background: none;
                    border: none;
                    color: blue;
                    cursor: pointer;
                    padding: 5px 0;
                    font-size: 0.9em;
                    text-decoration: underline;
                }
            </style>

            <div class="header-container">
                <span class="toggle-icon" id="toggleIcon">+</span>
                <span class="header-text" id="headerSlot"></span>
            </div>

            <div class="content-wrapper">
                <!-- Intro part is always visible -->
                <div class="intro-part" id="introSlot"></div>

                <!-- Details part is conditionally visible -->
                <div class="details-part" id="detailsSlot" style="display: none;"></div>

                <!-- Expand button visible only when collapsed -->
                <button class="expand-button" id="expandButton" style="display: none;">Expand more</button>
            </div>
        `;
    }

    // Updates the DOM based on the internal state (_expanded)
    updateView() {
        const headerSlot = this.shadowRoot.getElementById('headerSlot');
        const introSlot = this.shadowRoot.getElementById('introSlot');
        const detailsSlot = this.shadowRoot.getElementById('detailsSlot');
        const toggleIcon = this.shadowRoot.getElementById('toggleIcon');
        const expandButton = this.shadowRoot.getElementById('expandButton');

        // 1. Populate Slots (Requires getting content passed via custom attributes or children)
        // Since slot usage requires knowing which child goes where, we map children here.
        this.mapSlots(headerSlot, introSlot, detailsSlot);

        // 2. Update UI based on expanded state
        if (this._expanded) {
            // Expanded State
            toggleIcon.textContent = '−';
            detailsSlot.style.display = 'block';
            expandButton.style.display = 'none';
            // Ensure intro is always visible (it is by default)
        } else {
            // Collapsed State
            toggleIcon.textContent = '+';
            detailsSlot.style.display = 'none';
            expandButton.style.display = 'block';
        }
    }

    // Helper to map children into their respective slots
    mapSlots(headerSlot, introSlot, detailsSlot) {
        const children = Array.from(this.children);
        let headerContent = null;
        let introContent = null;
        let detailsContent = null;

        // Simple slot identification based on attribute presence in the child tag
        children.forEach(child => {
            if (child.hasAttribute('slot="header"')) {
                headerContent = child;
            } else if (child.hasAttribute('slot="intro"')) {
                introContent = child;
            } else if (child.hasAttribute('slot="details"')) {
                detailsContent = child;
            }
        });

        // Inject content (cloning is important to avoid modifying the original DOM structure)
        headerSlot.innerHTML = headerContent ? headerContent.innerHTML : '';
        introSlot.innerHTML = introContent ? introContent.innerHTML : '';
        detailsSlot.innerHTML = detailsContent ? detailsContent.innerHTML : '';
    }
}

// Define the custom element
customElements.define('x-details', XDetails);
```

### How to Use It (HTML Example)

Save the JavaScript above as `x-details.js` and include it in your HTML file.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>X-Details Component</title>
    <script src="x-details.js" defer></script>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>Custom X-Details Example</h1>

    <x-details>
        <span slot="header">Product Feature Overview</span>
        <div slot="intro">
            <strong>Key Benefit:</strong> This feature simplifies your workflow by automating repetitive tasks. See how it works below!
        </div>
        <div slot="details">
            Detailed technical specifications, compatibility matrix, and usage guides are available here. This content is hidden until expanded.
        </div>
    </x-details>

    <x-details>
        <span slot="header">Installation Guide</span>
        <div slot="intro">
            <strong>Quick Start:</strong> Simply run `npm install x-details` and include the component.
        </div>
        <div slot="details">
            For advanced setup, consult the full documentation on our developer portal. Dependencies list follows...
        </div>
    </x-details>

</body>
</html>
```

### Explanation of Key Features

1.  **Shadow DOM:** `this.attachShadow({ mode: 'open' })` encapsulates all component styling and structure, preventing CSS leakage.
2.  **Slot Handling:** The `mapSlots` method iterates over the component's children and uses the `slot` attribute (`slot="header"`, etc.) to determine which piece of content goes into which placeholder (`#headerSlot`, `#introSlot`, etc.) inside the Shadow DOM.
3.  **State Management:** The `_expanded` boolean tracks the state. `connectedCallback` sets up the click listener on the toggle area.
4.  **Conditional Rendering:**
    *   The **Intro Part** (`.intro-part`) is always displayed.
    *   The **Details Part** (`.details-part`) is hidden by default (`style="display: none;"`).
    *   The **"Expand more" button** is visible only when `_expanded` is `false`.
5.  **Styling:** The required styling (bottom border on the header, larger font, square `+`/`-` icon) is implemented within the component's internal `<style>` tag.

